# Cursor Rules for miataru iOS App

## Project Context
This is an open-source iOS application for privacy-friendly location tracking, sharing, and device management. Built with SwiftUI and modern iOS frameworks (iOS 18 and iOS 26).

## Code Style & Standards
- Use SwiftUI best practices
- Follow iOS Human Interface Guidelines
- Maintain privacy-first approach
- Use English for all code comments and strings
- Implement proper error handling and battery optimization

## Architecture Guidelines
- Use ObservableObject and @Published for state management
- Keep views lightweight and delegate business logic to managers
- Implement proper MVVM pattern
- Use UserDefaults for settings persistence
- Handle location permissions gracefully

## Key Components
- LocationManager: Handles location tracking and permissions
- SettingsManager: Manages user preferences
- Device management and QR code functionality
- Multi-platform support (iPhone, iPad, Mac)

## Development Workflow
- Test on multiple device types
- Consider battery optimization
- Maintain privacy compliance
- Follow iOS app store guidelines

## Common Patterns
- Use @StateObject for view models
- Implement proper onboarding flow
- Handle background/foreground transitions
- Manage device identifiers securely
